{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Culture, Myths, and Legends"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Writing a Short Narrative"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "  Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le11ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Writing in the Unreal Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to write about a hypothetical situation in the past, you use the Past Perfect tense. You can also use the word <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">wish </span>to talk about things that didn't happen, but you wanted to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If only I hadn't kissed the frog</span>. (= I did and it was a mistake because he turned into a horrible prince, but I can't change it now.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">What if the elephant had stepped on the mouse? </span> <br/>(She didn't, but we can imagine the result!)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb <span class=\"strong\"> to wish </span>is followed by the Past Perfect tense when we want to talk about situations in the present that we are not happy about but can't change."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I wish I had more money. (=but I haven't)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I had more to give you but we are simple people."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I was less trusting."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wish I was a more forgiving person."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only the family had known what darkness would befall their wintery home. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only I hadn't been so welcoming to the visitor."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If only I had been a stronger man I would have kept you close."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "igloo"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a house made of blocks of snow or ice in the form of a dome"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A long time ago, a young stranger entered a family igloo."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in myths and legends."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "canine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to dogs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:He wore a necklace with two large canine teeth."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "caribou"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a large type of deer that lives in northern parts of the world"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Anyone who braves this weather is considered a friend and is provided with caribou stew."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tracks"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a mark left on the ground by a moving animal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: All that remained were animal tracks outside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to paddle"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move a boat forward through water with a paddle"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The father paddled his daughter to a small island where he abandoned her."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pregnant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a baby"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To everyone's horror, his daughter became pregnant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "seal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large animal that lives in the sea near coasts, has flippers, and eats fish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These fingers became seals in the sea. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "walrus"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large animal that lives on land and in the sea in northern regions and that has flippers and long tusks"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She tried once again and he cut off her hands, which became walruses."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "forearm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the part of the arm between the elbow and the wrist"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She made one last daring attempt to climb aboard the boat but her father cut off her forearms."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "whale"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an often very large animal that lives in the ocean and that is a mammal rather than a fish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They turned into whales."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le11ob08aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to your local library and research other Inuit legends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose one legend that you are interested in. Does the legend talk about caribou, seals or whales?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write half a page of notes on what the legend is about. Who are the characters? What happens?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now write a paragraph in your own words based on the legend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraph to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research Inuit legends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write notes on the legend and then use those notes to write a paragraph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read the paragraph about a legend to a partner."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Narrative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">narrative</span> is a story. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "It uses a sequence of events to tell the story.<br/>The story is told by a narrator in either the 1st person (about their experience), or the 3rd person (about someone else's experience). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A narrative paints a picture of the events  through the use of character, setting and plot.<br/>These are enhanced by the use of descriptive words and phrases (adjective and adverb)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Folktales and fairytales are classic narratives."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Parts of a Narrative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Character\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"person or thing with human characteristics in a story\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Setting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"where the story happens\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Plot\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the storyline featuring a beginning, middle and end\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le11ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le11ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le11ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "A long time ago, a young stranger entered a family igloo wearing a necklace with two large canine teeth. \u201cAnyone who braves this weather is considered a friend and is provided with caribou stew and a place to lay their head. I wish I had more to give you but we are a simple people\u201d, the father said. The stranger was also given a slice of bread  by one of the daughters.  If only the family had known what darkness would befall their wintery home.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le11ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The following morning, the young man was gone. All that remained were animal tracks outside. The father exclaimed, \"We were deceived. That must have been my lead dog disguised as a man. I wish I was less trusting.\" To everyone's horror, his daughter became pregnant. \u201cIf only I hadn't been so welcoming to the visitor,\u201c he mumbled to his wife. The father paddled his daughter to a small island where he abandoned her. Later that summer, the father returned to the island.", "id": 2, "time": "26000", "image": "engenn10le11ob08re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "A storm threatened to capsize the overloaded vessel on their return. A crewman yelled to the father, \u201cI have worked on ships all my life but I am terrified.\u201d The father decided that to lighten the load they must throw the daughter overboard. When she tried to climb back into the boat, her father cut off her fingers. These fingers became seals in the sea. She tried once again and he cut off her hands, which became walruses. She made one last daring attempt to climb aboard the boat but her father cut off her forearms, which transformed into whales.\n<br/>", "id": 3, "time": "58000", "image": "engenn10le11ob08re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "The girl sank into the depths of the sea. Her father cried out, \u201cIf only I had been a stronger man I would have kept you close.\u201d His daughter was given control of  all sea beasts by a special power. She is half-woman and half-fish.", "id": 4, "time": "93000", "image": "engenn10le11ob08re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "video", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn10le10ob08re3vid01", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "Writing a Short Narrative", "id": 1, "time": "5000", "image": ""}, {"text": "<span class = \"bullet\">What is a legend?</span>", "id": 2, "time": "10000", "image": ""}, {"text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Narratives</span>", "id": 3, "time": "44000", "image": ""}, {"text": "<span class = \"bullet\">What should a narrative include?</span>", "id": 4, "time": "60000", "image": ""}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write a short narrative."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about myths and legends in different cultures."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can write about past situations that did not happen. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "  Why do you think people keep legends alive?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "  How important do you think myths and legends are to a society?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": 